window.VAMP_SEARCH = [{"page": "Vamp documentation", "title": "Vamp documentation", "url": "index.html", "text": "Vamp documentation Vamp is a compiled programming language for Windows. Programs are compiled through LLVM into small native .exe files that run at speeds comparable to C and C++, while memory is managed automatically. Copy class Player : ( val name : str val health : int func hit ( damage : int ) : ( self . health -= damage ) ) val hero = Player ( \"Ryan\" , 100 ) hero . hit ( 25 ) println ( f\"{ hero . name } has { hero . health } health\" )"}, {"page": "Vamp documentation", "title": "Install", "url": "index.html#install", "text": "Download Vamp-<version>-x64.msi from the releases page and run it. It installs Vamp for the current user, sets up the Visual Studio Code extension and adds vamp to the PATH . On the last page, leave Download and install LLVM and the C++ build tools selected if they are not installed yet; Vamp requires them to build programs. They can also be installed later with vamp setup . Open a new terminal and run a program: Copy vamp run hello.vp"}, {"page": "Vamp documentation", "title": "Your first program", "url": "index.html#your-first-program", "text": "Save this as hello.vp : Copy val name : str = \"Vamp\" func greet ( person : str , times : int = 1 ) : ( for ( n ) in ( range ( times )) : ( println ( \"Hello \" + person ) ) ) println ( f\"Hello from { name }!\" ) greet ( \"Jake\" , 2 ) vamp run hello.vp builds hello.exe next to the file and runs it. vamp hello.vp only builds it."}, {"page": "Vamp documentation", "title": "Where to go next", "url": "index.html#where-to-go-next", "text": "Language basics Types, variables, functions, control flow and strings. Classes and types Classes, inheritance, interfaces, generics and optionals. Collections Lists, maps, sets, tuples and slices. Standard libraries Math, files, JSON, threads, networking, regex and more. Windows and interfaces Native windows, controls, events and drawing. Tools The vamp command, VS Code, debugging and packages."}, {"page": "Source files and comments", "title": "Source files and comments", "url": "source-files-and-comments.html", "text": "Vamp source files use the .vp extension. Strings go in double quotes. Inside a string, \\n is a new line, \\t a tab, \\\" a quote and \\\\ a backslash. Any other backslash is kept as written, so \"C:\\Users\\me\" works as expected. The exception is a path piece that starts with n or t ( \"C:\\new\" ), or a string ending in a backslash: write \\\\ there. Copy // line comment /* block comment */"}, {"page": "Types, variables, and constants", "title": "Types, variables, and constants", "url": "types-variables-and-constants.html", "text": "The most common types are int , float , bool and str . int and float are the largest and most precise, and are the recommended defaults. The fixed-size types are intended for cases where size matters, such as large lists or binary file formats. Type Holds int (or i64 ) Whole numbers, 64-bit, signed (roughly ±9.2 × 10¹⁸). i8 , i16 , i32 Signed whole numbers, 8, 16 and 32 bits. u8 , u16 , u32 , u64 Unsigned whole numbers, 8, 16, 32 and 64 bits. float (or double ) 64-bit decimal, about 15 significant digits. f32 32-bit decimal, about 7 significant digits. char One byte, in single quotes: 'A' , '\\n' . bool true or false . str Text. Copy val population : int = 8000000000 val level : u8 = 200 val precise : float = 3.141592653589793 val letter : char = 'A' val mask : int = 0xFF // hex; 0b1010 is binary val distance : float = 1.5e8 // 150000000.0; 2e-3 is 0.002 A number literal takes the type it is used with, so val small : i32 = 5 and small + 1 need no conversion. A literal that does not fit ( val level : u8 = 300 ) will not compile. Values of two different number types are never mixed implicitly; convert one side, for example int(small) + count . i64 and int are the same type, and so are double and float , so they mix freely. A whole-number literal too large for int is a u64 . Copy val count : int = 10 const title : str = \"Vamp\" val declares a mutable variable. const declares an immutable constant and requires both a type and a value. A single val can omit its type when the value determines it. A typed val with no value starts with the default value: 0 , 0.0 , false , \"\" , an empty list or map, or a struct with every field set to zero. A variable declared at the top of a file (outside any function, loop or if ) is global. Every function in the file can read and modify it, including functions declared above it. Several variables of the same type can be declared together: Copy val x , y , z : int = 10 , 20 , 30 val first , second , third : int When values are given, there m"}, {"page": "Expressions and assignment", "title": "Expressions and assignment", "url": "expressions-and-assignment.html", "text": "Operators Description + - * / % Arithmetic. % is the remainder and -x negates. == != < <= > >= Comparison, producing a bool . Strings compare alphabetically; booleans and enums support only == and != . and or not Logical operators on bool values. and and or stop as soon as the result is known, so the right side may not run. && \\|\\| ! The same operators written as symbols: && is and , \\|\\| is or , ! is not . Either form can be used. & \\| ^ ~ << >> Bitwise and, or, xor, not, shift left, shift right, on whole numbers. Precedence, from lowest to highest: or || , and && , not , comparisons, | , ^ , & , << >> , + - , * / % , then unary - ! ~ . Use parentheses when in doubt. not applies to the whole comparison after it, so not lives == 0 means not (lives == 0) . ! applies only to the value immediately after it, so it requires parentheses: !(lives == 0) . Copy if ( lives > 0 and not paused ) : ( println ( \"playing\" ) ) if ( lives > 0 && ! paused ) : ( println ( \"playing\" ) ) // equivalent val low_bits : int = flags & 0x0F val even : bool = count % 2 == 0 Variables, fields and elements can be updated with = , += , -= , *= , /= , %= , &= , |= , ^= , <<= and >>= : Copy count += 1 player . score *= 2 scores [ 0 ] -= 5 Whole-number division or % by zero throws an error ( division by zero ), which can be caught with try ."}, {"page": "Expressions and assignment", "title": "Picking a value: a if condition else b", "url": "expressions-and-assignment.html#picking-a-value-a-if-condition-else-b", "text": "Copy val label : str = \"big\" if size > 100 else \"small\" val speed : float = 2.5 if boosted else 1 Both sides must have the same type. A number literal on one side takes the type of the other. + also concatenates strings: Copy println ( \"count: \" + str ( count ))"}, {"page": "Functions and returns", "title": "Functions and returns", "url": "functions-and-returns.html", "text": "Functions take named, typed parameters, and the body is written in the second pair of parentheses: Copy func add ( left : int , right : int ) : ( return : int ( left + right ) ) func announce () : ( println ( \"Ready\" ) return : void ) return : type (expression) returns a value, return : void returns nothing. A function that returns a value must return on every path; a function that returns nothing may simply end. The return type can also be written in the header, between the parameters and the body: Copy func average ( left : float , right : float ) : float : ( return : float (( left + right ) / 2.0 ) ) Parameters and results can be any type. Numbers, strings and structs are copied. Classes, lists and maps are shared."}, {"page": "Functions and returns", "title": "Default values", "url": "functions-and-returns.html#default-values", "text": "A parameter with = value can be omitted by callers. Parameters with defaults must come last. Copy func greet ( name : str , times : int = 1 ) : ( for ( n ) in ( range ( times )) : ( println ( \"Hello \" + name ) ) ) greet ( \"Emma\" ) greet ( \"Emma\" , 3 )"}, {"page": "Functions and returns", "title": "Overloading", "url": "functions-and-returns.html#overloading", "text": "Functions can share a name when their parameter types differ. The call selects the version that matches the arguments. Copy func show ( value : int ) : ( println ( \"number \" + str ( value )) ) func show ( value : str ) : ( println ( \"text \" + value ) ) show ( 3 ) show ( \"three\" ) A function can be called before the line that declares it."}, {"page": "Functions and returns", "title": "Functions as values", "url": "functions-and-returns.html#functions-as-values", "text": "Functions can be stored in variables, passed as arguments and returned. The type is func(parameter types) : result type ; omit : result type for a function that returns nothing. Copy func twice ( x : int ) : int : ( return : int ( x * 2 ) ) func apply ( f : func ( int ) : int , value : int ) : int : ( return : int ( f ( value )) ) println ( apply ( twice , 21 )) // 42 val greet : func ( str ) = func ( name : str ) : ( println ( \"hi \" + name ) ) greet ( \"Jake\" ) func (parameters) : type : ( body ) without a name is a function written inline. It can use the surrounding local variables: it keeps its own copy of each one, taken when it is created, and changes it makes to that copy persist between calls. Copy func make_counter () : func () : int : ( val count : int = 0 return : func () : int ( func () : int : ( count += 1 return : int ( count ) )) ) val next_id = make_counter () next_id () println ( next_id ()) // 2 Top-level variables are shared rather than copied, so changing one inside a function value changes it everywhere."}, {"page": "Functions and returns", "title": "Generic functions", "url": "functions-and-returns.html#generic-functions", "text": "Square brackets after the name list type parameters. The types are inferred from the arguments, or can be written explicitly at the call. Copy func biggest [ T ]( a : T , b : T ) : T : ( return : T ( a if a > b else b ) ) println ( biggest ( 3 , 9 )) // 9 println ( biggest ( \"pear\" , \"apple\" )) // pear println ( biggest [ float ]( 1 , 2 )) // 2.000000 Each combination of types is compiled separately, so generic code is as fast as code written for a single type."}, {"page": "Functions and returns", "title": "Returning several values: tuples", "url": "functions-and-returns.html#returning-several-values-tuples", "text": "(T, U) is a tuple type: a fixed group of values. A function can return one, and the caller can unpack it into several names. Copy func divide ( a : int , b : int ) : ( int , int ) : ( return : ( int , int ) ( a / b , a % b ) ) val quotient , remainder = divide ( 17 , 5 ) val pair = ( 1 , \"one\" ) println ( pair [ 1 ]) // one Elements are read with a constant index such as pair[0] . Tuples cannot be modified after creation."}, {"page": "Control flow", "title": "if, else if, else", "url": "control-flow.html#if-else-if-else", "text": "Copy if ( score >= 90 ) : ( println ( \"A\" ) ) else if ( score >= 80 ) : ( println ( \"B\" ) ) else : ( println ( \"Keep practicing\" ) ) Conditions must be bool expressions."}, {"page": "Control flow", "title": "while loops", "url": "control-flow.html#while-loops", "text": "Copy val remaining : int = 3 while ( remaining > 0 ) : ( println ( remaining ) remaining -= 1 ) The condition is checked before each iteration."}, {"page": "Control flow", "title": "for loops", "url": "control-flow.html#for-loops", "text": "Copy val names = [ \"Emma\" , \"Jake\" ] for ( name ) in ( names ) : ( println ( name ) ) Arrays are iterated in index order. Iterating over a dictionary yields its field names in declaration order, and dictionary.values yields the values in that order. A for loop also iterates over lists (elements), maps (keys, in the order they were added) and strings (characters, as char ). Use range to count: Copy for ( i ) in ( range ( 5 )) : ( println ( i ) ) // 0 1 2 3 4 for ( i ) in ( range ( 2 , 6 )) : ( println ( i ) ) // 2 3 4 5 for ( i ) in ( range ( 10 , 0 , - 2 )) : ( println ( i ) ) // 10 8 6 4 2 range(stop) , range(start, stop) and range(start, stop, step) take int values; stop itself is not included."}, {"page": "Control flow", "title": "break and continue", "url": "control-flow.html#break-and-continue", "text": "In any while or for loop, break exits the loop and continue skips to the next iteration. Copy for ( name ) in ( names ) : ( if ( name == \"\" ) : ( continue ) if ( name == \"stop\" ) : ( break ) println ( name ) )"}, {"page": "Control flow", "title": "match", "url": "control-flow.html#match", "text": "match compares a value against the patterns of each branch in order and runs the first branch that matches. A branch can list several patterns. else is optional and must come last; without it, a value that matches no pattern runs nothing. Copy match ( key ) : ( \"w\" , \"up\" : ( move ( 0 , - 1 ) ) \"s\" , \"down\" : ( move ( 0 , 1 ) ) else : ( println ( \"unknown key\" ) ) ) The value can be a number, str , char , bool or enum, and the patterns must be of the same type."}, {"page": "Strings", "title": "Strings", "url": "strings.html", "text": "+ joins strings, and str(value) turns any number, bool , char or enum into text. text[index] reads one character as a char . len(text) is the length in bytes. Method Result text.length() Length in bytes. text.upper() , text.lower() Upper or lower case copy. text.trim() Copy with spaces, tabs and new lines cut off both ends. text.contains(part) , text.starts_with(part) , text.ends_with(part) bool . text.find(part) Index of the first match, or -1 . text.replace(from, to) Copy with every from swapped for to . text.split(separator) The pieces as a list[str] . An empty separator splits into single characters. text.substring(start, count) count characters starting at start ; a negative count means \"to the end\". text.repeat(times) , text.reverse() Repeated or reversed copy ( reverse keeps characters like é in one piece). text.char_at(index) Same as text[index] . text.is_number() Whether int(...) or float(...) can convert it. text.char_count() Number of characters, counting multi-byte ones like é once. text.chars() A list[str] with one entry per character (UTF-8 aware). text.code_points() Each character's Unicode number, as a list[int] . Copy val line : str = \" name = Emma \" val parts = line . trim (). split ( \" = \" ) println ( parts [ 1 ]. upper ()) // EMMA String methods always return a new string and never modify the original. text[start:end] slices text the same way as lists."}, {"page": "Strings", "title": "Formatted strings", "url": "strings.html#formatted-strings", "text": "Prefixing a string with f allows values to be inserted with { } . Any expression can be used, optionally followed by a format after : : a width, an alignment ( < left, > right, ^ centre) and, for floats, how many decimals. Copy val name : str = \"Emma\" val price : float = 3.14159 println ( f\"{ name } owes { price :. 2 }\" ) // Emma owes 3.14 println ( f\"|{ name : < 6 }|{ price : > 8.1 }|\" ) // |Emma | 3.1| println ( f\"{ { braces }} and { name . upper () }\" ) // {braces} and EMMA {{ and }} produce literal braces. Quotes inside the braces are written \\\" , same as anywhere else in a string."}, {"page": "Strings", "title": "Building long text", "url": "strings.html#building-long-text", "text": "Joining many pieces with + copies the entire text each time. A builder collects the pieces and builds the text once: Copy val report = builder () for ( i ) in ( range ( 1000 )) : ( report . add_line ( f\"row { i }\" ) ) println ( report . text (). length ()) add(value) appends any value (numbers and other types are converted), add_line(value) also appends a new line ( add_line() alone adds only the new line), text() returns the text, length() its length and clear() empties it."}, {"page": "Enums", "title": "Enums", "url": "enums.html", "text": "An enum is a type with a fixed set of named values. Copy enum State : ( Menu Playing Paused = 10 Over ) val state : State = State . Menu state = State . Playing match ( state ) : ( State . Menu : ( println ( \"menu\" ) ) State . Playing , State . Paused : ( println ( \"in game\" ) ) ) println ( state ) // Playing println ( int ( state )) // 1 Values count up from 0 . = number sets a value explicitly, and later members continue from it. Enums compare with == and != , print as their name, and convert with int(...) and str(...) ."}, {"page": "Arrays and dictionaries", "title": "Arrays", "url": "arrays-and-dictionaries.html#arrays", "text": "Copy val names = [ \"Emma\" , \"Jake\" , \"Lucy\" ] println ( names [ 0 ]) Arrays hold one type and have a fixed size. Elements can be read and written by index, but indexes are not bounds-checked and must be valid. For checked indexes and a variable size, use a list ."}, {"page": "Arrays and dictionaries", "title": "Dictionaries", "url": "arrays-and-dictionaries.html#dictionaries", "text": "Copy val person = { Name : str = \"Emma\" , Age : int = 31 } println ( person . Name ) for ( field_name ) in ( person ) : ( println ( field_name ) ) for ( field_value ) in ( person . values ) : ( println ( field_value ) ) A dictionary is a record with fixed fields. Each field has a name and a type and is accessed with dictionary.FieldName . Arrays and dictionaries are stored inline, without extra allocation."}, {"page": "Lists and maps", "title": "Lists and maps", "url": "lists-and-maps.html", "text": "Arrays and dictionaries have a fixed size, while lists and maps grow and shrink as the program runs. They are declared with their type and filled with the same [ ] and { } literals."}, {"page": "Lists and maps", "title": "Lists", "url": "lists-and-maps.html#lists", "text": "Copy val scores : list [ int ] = [ 10 , 20 ] val names : list [ str ] = [] scores . push ( 30 ) scores [ 0 ] = 15 println ( scores [ 2 ]) println ( scores . length ()) for ( score ) in ( scores ) : ( println ( score ) ) Method Result list.push(value) Adds a value at the end. list.pop() Removes and returns the last value. list.insert(index, value) Inserts before index , shifting the rest up. list.remove(index) Removes the value at index . list.clear() Removes every value. list.length() , len(list) The number of values. list.is_empty() Whether the list has no values. list.first() , list.last() First or last value. list.contains(value) Whether the list contains the value. list.index_of(value) Index of the first match, or -1 . list.sort() Sorts numbers low to high and strings alphabetically. list.reverse() Reverses the order. list.copy() A separate list with the same values. list.join(separator) For list[str] : one string with separator between the values. list.filter(keep) A new list with the values where keep(value) is true . list.map(change) A new list of change(value) for each value; the element type is the type returned by change . list.for_each(action) Calls action(value) on each value. list.any(test) , list.all(test) Whether test(value) is true for at least one value, or for all of them. list.find_index(test) Index of the first value where test(value) is true , or -1 . list.reduce(combine, start) Folds the list into one value, calling combine(total, value) for each value, starting from start . list.sort_by(comes_first) Sorts using a custom order: comes_first(a, b) returns true when a should come before b . Stable. Elements can be of any type, including structs, classes and other lists ( list[list[int]] ). Reading or writing an index that does not exist raises an error that reports the index and the length, which can be caught with try ."}, {"page": "Lists and maps", "title": "Maps", "url": "lists-and-maps.html#maps", "text": "A map stores a value for each key. Keys can be str , char or any whole-number type. Copy val ages : map [ str , int ] = { \"Emma\" : 31 , \"Jake\" : 27 } ages [ \"Lucy\" ] = 24 ages [ \"Emma\" ] += 1 if ( ages . has ( \"Jake\" )) : ( println ( ages [ \"Jake\" ]) ) println ( ages . get ( \"Nobody\" , 0 )) for ( name ) in ( ages ) : ( println ( name + \" is \" + str ( ages [ name ])) ) Method Result map[key] = value , map.set(key, value) Adds the key or replaces its value. map[key] The value for that key. A missing key raises an error (catchable with try ). map.get(key, fallback) The value, or fallback if the key is not there. map.has(key) Whether the key is present. map.remove(key) Removes the key; returns whether it existed. map.length() , len(map) The number of keys. map.is_empty() , map.clear() As for lists. map.keys() , map.values() New lists of the keys or values, in the order the keys were added. Lists and maps are shared, not copied: passing one to a function or assigning it to another variable creates a second reference to the same object. Use list.copy() when a separate copy is needed. Copy val scores : list [ int ] = [ 7 , 2 , 9 , 4 ] val high = scores . filter ( func ( s : int ) : bool : ( return : bool ( s > 5 ) )) // [7, 9] val labels = scores . map ( func ( s : int ) : str : ( return : str ( f\"#{ s }\" ) )) // [\"#7\", \"#2\", ...] scores . sort_by ( func ( a : int , b : int ) : bool : ( return : bool ( a > b ) )) // highest first println ( scores [ 1 : 3 ]) // [7, 4] list[start:end] is a new list from start up to, but not including, end . Either side can be left out ( xs[:2] , xs[2:] ), and negative numbers count from the end ( xs[-2:] is the last two)."}, {"page": "Lists and maps", "title": "Sets", "url": "lists-and-maps.html#sets", "text": "A set holds each value at most once, in the order the values were first added. Values can be str , char or whole numbers. Copy val seen : set [ str ] = {} seen . add ( \"Emma\" ) seen . add ( \"Emma\" ) println ( seen . length ()) // 1 val primes = { 2 , 3 , 5 , 7 } val odd : set [ int ] = { 1 , 3 , 5 , 7 , 9 } println ( primes . intersection ( odd )) // {3, 5, 7} Method Result set.add(value) , set.remove(value) Adds a value, or removes it (returns whether it was there). set.has(value) , set.contains(value) Whether the value is in the set. set.length() , len(set) , set.is_empty() , set.clear() As for lists. set.union(other) , set.intersection(other) , set.difference(other) New sets. set.is_subset(other) Whether every value is also in other . set.values() , set.copy() The values as a list, or a separate copy of the set. A for loop iterates over a set's values. println prints lists, maps, sets and tuples in the same form they are written: [1, 2] , {\"Emma\": 31} , (1, \"one\") ."}, {"page": "Classes", "title": "Classes", "url": "classes.html", "text": "A class declares fields, methods and, optionally, nested classes. Class values are references: assigning one to another variable or passing it to a function creates a second reference to the same object, as in Python, Java and C#. Copy class Car : ( val brand : str const max_speed : int class Engine : ( const horsepower : int ) func speed_with_bonus ( bonus : int ) : ( return : int ( self . max_speed + bonus ) ) ) val car = Car ( \"Vamp\" , 200 ) val engine = car . Engine ( 450 ) println ( car . speed_with_bonus ( 10 )) println ( engine . horsepower ) The constructor takes the fields in declaration order. Methods receive self implicitly and are called with object.method(arguments) . A nested class is constructed through an instance of the enclosing class. val fields can be assigned ( car.brand = \"Other\" , or self.brand = \"Other\" inside a method). const fields cannot be changed."}, {"page": "Classes", "title": "Inheritance", "url": "classes.html#inheritance", "text": "class Child(Parent) inherits every field and method of Parent and can add its own. The constructor takes the parent's fields first. Redeclaring a method in the child overrides it, and super.method(...) calls the parent's version from inside the child. Copy class Animal : ( val name : str func sound () : str : ( return : str ( \"...\" ) ) func describe () : str : ( return : str ( self . name + \" says \" + self . sound ()) ) ) class Dog ( Animal ) : ( val breed : str func sound () : str : ( return : str ( \"Woof\" ) ) func parent_sound () : str : ( return : str ( super . sound ()) ) ) val dog = Dog ( \"Max\" , \"Beagle\" ) println ( dog . sound ()) // Woof println ( dog . name ) // Max The method that runs depends on the object, not the variable, so a Dog stored in a list[Animal] still barks. A child object can be used wherever its parent class is expected. Copy val pets : list [ Animal ] = [ Dog ( \"Max\" , \"Beagle\" ), Animal ( \"Rocky\" )] for ( pet ) in ( pets ) : ( println ( pet . sound ()) ) // Woof, then ... == and != on class values compare identity: whether both refer to the same object."}, {"page": "Classes", "title": "Interfaces", "url": "classes.html#interfaces", "text": "An interface lists methods without bodies. A class names the interfaces it implements after its parent (or on their own) and must provide every method they list. Copy interface Shape : ( func area () : float func name () : str ) class Circle ( Shape ) : ( val radius : float func area () : float : ( return : float ( 3.14159 * self . radius * self . radius ) ) func name () : str : ( return : str ( \"circle\" ) ) ) class Square ( Shape ) : ( val side : float func area () : float : ( return : float ( self . side * self . side ) ) func name () : str : ( return : str ( \"square\" ) ) ) val shapes : list [ Shape ] = [ Circle ( 1.0 ), Square ( 2.0 )] for ( shape ) in ( shapes ) : ( println ( f\"{ shape . name () }: { shape . area ():. 2 }\" ) ) class Button(Control, Clickable, Drawable) extends the class Control and implements two interfaces."}, {"page": "Classes", "title": "Overloaded methods, operators and printing", "url": "classes.html#overloaded-methods-operators-and-printing", "text": "Methods can share a name when their parameter types differ, as with functions. A method named after an operator defines that operator for the class or struct: + - * / % take one value, == != < <= > >= take one value and return bool , and func -() with no parameters is negation. If only == is defined, != is its negation. Copy struct Vec : ( val x : float val y : float func + ( other : Vec ) : Vec : ( return : Vec ( Vec ( self . x + other . x , self . y + other . y )) ) func * ( factor : float ) : Vec : ( return : Vec ( Vec ( self . x * factor , self . y * factor )) ) func to_str () : str : ( return : str ( f\"({ self . x }, { self . y })\" ) ) ) val v = Vec ( 1 , 2 ) + Vec ( 3 , 4 ) * 2 println ( v ) func to_str() : str controls how a value is displayed by println , str(...) and f-strings. Without it, a class or struct prints its fields: Vec(x = 7.000000, y = 10.000000) ."}, {"page": "Classes", "title": "Iterators", "url": "classes.html#iterators", "text": "A for loop can iterate over any class with a next() method that returns T? . The loop continues until next() returns none . Copy class Countdown : ( val current : int func next () : int ? : ( if ( self . current <= 0 ) : ( return : int ? ( none ) ) self . current -= 1 return : int ? ( self . current + 1 ) ) ) for ( n ) in ( Countdown ( 3 )) : ( print ( n ) ) // 321"}, {"page": "Classes", "title": "Generic classes and structs", "url": "classes.html#generic-classes-and-structs", "text": "Type parameters also work on classes and structs. The types can be written explicitly ( Stack[int] ) or inferred from the constructor values. Copy class Stack [ T ] : ( val items : list [ T ] func push ( value : T ) : ( self . items . push ( value ) ) func pop () : T : ( return : T ( self . items . pop ()) ) ) struct Pair [ A , B ] : ( val first : A val second : B ) val numbers = Stack [ int ]([]) numbers . push ( 1 ) val reading : Pair [ str , float ] = Pair ( \"pi\" , 3.14 )"}, {"page": "Classes", "title": "Structs", "url": "classes.html#structs", "text": "A struct is a record of fields and can have methods. Unlike a class, a struct is a value and is copied when assigned or passed. Copy struct Point : ( val x : int val y : int ) val start = Point ( 1 , 2 ) start . x = 10 func moved ( point : Point , by : int ) : Point : ( point . x += by return : Point ( point ) ) val end = moved ( start , 5 ) // start doesn't change val origin : Point // every field zero Assigning, passing, returning or storing a struct in a list creates a copy. A method on a struct operates on the variable it is called on, so point.move(1, 2) changes point . Structs and classes can be fields of other structs and classes ( val corner : Point ), list elements ( list[Point] ) and map values. Structs do not support inheritance."}, {"page": "Optional values and none", "title": "Optional values and none", "url": "optional-values-and-none.html", "text": "T? is either a T or none . Fields, variables, parameters and return values can be optional. Copy class Node : ( val value : int val next : Node ? ) val head = Node ( 1 , Node ( 2 , Node ( 3 , none ))) val current : Node ? = head while ( current != none ) : ( println ( current . value ) current = current . next ) func find ( items : list [ str ], wanted : str ) : int ? : ( for ( i ) in ( range ( items . length ())) : ( if ( items [ i ] == wanted ) : ( return : int ? ( i ) ) ) return : int ? ( none ) ) val position = find ([ \"a\" , \"b\" ], \"z\" ) println ( position . value_or ( - 1 )) // -1 A T can be used wherever a T? is expected. x == none and x != none check for a value, as does x.has_value() . x.value() returns the value and raises an error for none ; x.value_or(fallback) returns fallback instead. Fields and methods of an optional class or struct can be used directly ( current.value ); doing so on none raises a catchable error. A variable of a class type requires an object; declare it as Node? to allow it to start as none ."}, {"page": "Error handling", "title": "Error handling", "url": "error-handling.html", "text": "throw(message) raises an error. A try block runs its statements; if an error is raised inside it, including in functions it calls, the rest of the block is skipped and the catch block runs. The name in catch (name) receives the message as a str and can be omitted ( catch : ( ). Copy func withdraw ( balance : int , amount : int ) : int : ( if ( amount > balance ) : ( throw ( \"not enough money\" ) ) return : int ( balance - amount ) ) try : ( val left = withdraw ( 10 , 50 ) println ( left ) ) catch ( problem ) : ( println ( \"Could not withdraw: \" + problem ) ) Vamp raises its own errors in the same way, so they can be caught too: whole-number division or % by zero, an invalid list index, a missing map key, an invalid string index, list.pop() on an empty list, using a field or method on none , a file that cannot be read, invalid JSON, invalid text in int(...) , and others mentioned with each library. An uncaught error prints Error: message and exits with code 1 . assert(condition) raises an error when the condition is false ; assert(condition, \"message\") adds a custom message. The error includes the file and line."}, {"page": "Tests", "title": "Tests", "url": "tests.html", "text": "Tests are written in test \"name\" : ( ... ) blocks at the top level of a file. Normal builds exclude them. vamp test file.vp keeps the file's functions, classes and top-level variables, skips its other top-level code, runs each test separately and reports the result: Copy func add ( a : int , b : int ) : int : ( return : int ( a + b ) ) test \"adds numbers\" : ( assert ( add ( 2 , 3 ) == 5 ) assert ( add ( - 1 , 1 ) == 0 , \"negatives cancel\" ) ) Copy PASS adds numbers 1 test, 0 failed A failed assert or any uncaught error fails that test, and the remaining tests still run. vamp test exits with code 1 if any test failed."}, {"page": "Console output and program exit", "title": "Console output and program exit", "url": "console-output-and-program-exit.html", "text": "Copy print ( \"No newline\" ) println ( \"Line with newline\" ) exit ( 0 ) print writes without a trailing new line; println adds one. Both accept strings, every number type, bool , char and enums. exit(code) ends the program with the given exit code."}, {"page": "Imports", "title": "Imports", "url": "imports.html", "text": "Import a built-in library by name, or bind a source file to a name: Copy import os import helpers : \"helpers.vp\""}, {"page": "Imports", "title": "Renaming with as", "url": "imports.html#renaming-with-as", "text": "as gives a library or file a different name, as in Python: Copy import os as system import helpers : \"helpers.vp\" as h import \"helpers.vp\" as h2 system . Sleep ( 100 ) val total : int = h . add ( 2 , 3 ) Once a library is imported under another name, the original name is no longer bound ( os.Sleep(1) is an error suggesting system.Sleep(1) ). A file can be imported with import name : \"file.vp\" or with import \"file.vp\" (the name is the file name without .vp ); both forms accept as ."}, {"page": "Imports", "title": "Picking names with from", "url": "imports.html#picking-names-with-from", "text": "Copy from os import Sleep , Directory_Exists as exists from helpers : \"helpers.vp\" import add , twice as dbl , Point from os import * Sleep ( 100 ) val sum : int = add ( 1 , 2 ) from X import a, b as c binds only the listed names. from X import * binds every public name (names starting with _ are skipped). A from import does not bind the library or file name itself. Classes, structs, enums and interfaces can also be renamed: from shapes : \"shapes.vp\" import Point as P makes P a name for Point in types and calls. Rules that apply to every import: Imports must be at the top level of a file, not inside a function, loop or class. Two imports cannot bind the same name, and a function cannot reuse an imported name. Import paths are resolved relative to the importing file. A file imported twice is compiled once. Circular imports are an error that shows the full chain."}, {"page": "Imports", "title": "Importing Vamp files", "url": "imports.html#importing-vamp-files", "text": "An imported .vp file may contain only func , class , struct , enum and interface declarations, const constants, test blocks and imports. Classes, structs, enums and interfaces keep one global name across all files, so they are used by that name (or imported under another one). Functions and constants are namespaced per file, so add in helpers.vp never clashes with another add . Calls compile to direct calls, and functions that are never called are left out of the program. Copy import shapes : \"shapes.vp\" from shapes : \"shapes.vp\" import MAX_SIZE as LIMIT println ( shapes . MAX_SIZE ) println ( LIMIT )"}, {"page": "Imports", "title": "Packages", "url": "imports.html#packages", "text": "A package is a folder of Vamp files inside a vamp_packages folder in the project. vamp install downloads one with git, and it is imported with @ and its name. Copy vamp install https://github.com/someone/physics physics Copy import physics : \"@physics\" // vamp_packages/physics/physics.vp import shapes : \"@physics/shapes.vp\" // another file of the package Vamp looks for vamp_packages in the importing file's folder first, then in each folder above it. vamp packages lists the installed packages and vamp remove name deletes one."}, {"page": "Imports", "title": "Data files (.vpdata)", "url": "imports.html#data-files-vpdata", "text": "A .vpdata file lists the assets a program uses, such as models, textures, fonts, sounds and animations. Use one file per kind of asset, for example Models.vpdata , Textures.vpdata and Animations.vpdata . Each entry starts with object , a name in quotes, and its properties: Copy object \"player\" : ( type : \".obj\" , path : \"/objects/player.obj\" , size : ( 1 , 2 , 1 ), position : ( 0 , 0 , 0 ), scale : 1.5 , name : \"Player\" ) object \"tree\" : ( path : \"objects/tree.obj\" scale : 2.0 ) path is required. It is relative to the .vpdata file's folder (a leading / has the same meaning), and the file must exist at compile time. type is optional and defaults to the file extension ( \".obj\" above). All other properties are user-defined. A value can be text in quotes, a number, true / false , a group (x, y, z) or a list [a, b, c] . Groups and lists hold one kind of value; if whole numbers and decimals are mixed, all of them become float . Commas between properties are optional. Names follow the same rules as variable names, so code can refer to models.player . // and /* */ comments work as in .vp files. A data file is imported like a Vamp file. Each object becomes a constant struct with its properties as fields, plus id (its name), type , path and full_path (the absolute path, resolved at compile time): Copy import models : \"Models.vpdata\" println ( models . player . path ) // objects/player.obj println ( models . player . scale * 2 ) // 3.000000 println ( models . player . size ) // (1, 2, 1) for ( entry ) in ( models . all ()) : ( // every object, in file order println ( entry . id + \" \" + entry . type ) ) println ( models . names ()) // [\"player\", \"tree\"] val found = models . get ( \"tree\" ) // DataEntry?, none if there's no such object if ( found != none ) : ( println ( found . path ) ) all() returns a list[DataEntry] and get returns a DataEntry? . A DataEntry only has the four shared fields ( id , type , path , full_path ), since objects can have different properties. An object'"}, {"page": "Imports", "title": "Importing C and C++ libraries", "url": "imports.html#importing-c-and-c-libraries", "text": "A header or source file is imported like a Vamp file. Vamp asks clang for its declarations, so namespaces, overloads, inline and header-only code all work: Copy import mathlib : \"mathlib.hpp\" from mathlib : \"mathlib.hpp\" import is_even as even , greet val area : int = mathlib . area ( 3 , 4 ) // geo::area(int, int) val total : float = mathlib . add ( 1.5 , 2.5 ) // selects the float overload println ( even ( 10 )) println ( greet ( \"Vamp\" )) Supported extensions: .h .hh .hpp .hxx .c .cc .cpp .cxx . A source file with the same name next to it ( mathlib.cpp next to mathlib.hpp ) is compiled and linked automatically. To link a prebuilt library, add link \"name\" after the path: import sdl : \"SDL.h\" link \"SDL2\" links -lSDL2 . A value with a file extension, such as link \"libs/physics.lib\" , is passed as a file. Namespaces are flattened: geo::area becomes mathlib.area . Overloads are selected by the Vamp types of the arguments, which must match exactly. Type mapping: int ↔ any C integer type (passed as long long , then converted), float ↔ float or double , bool ↔ bool , str ↔ const char * or std::string (a returned std::string is copied into memory that is never freed automatically), plus void returns. Not yet supported: classes and structs, templates, global variables, enums, modifiable references ( int & ), pointers other than char * , and variadic functions. Attempting to use one produces an error that names it and explains how to wrap it in a plain function. A C++ exception that escapes an imported function prints its message and stops the program. Only functions that are called are compiled in, and each call is a single direct call."}, {"page": "Imports", "title": "Compiler error messages", "url": "imports.html#compiler-error-messages", "text": "Every error starts with file:line:column , shows the source line with a caret, and often ends with a hint: Copy main.vp:3:25: error: Library 'os' has no method named 'Slep' 3 | from os import Slep | ^^^^ hint: did you mean 'Sleep'? Errors inside an imported file name that file and add note: while importing ... lines showing the chain of imports."}, {"page": "Memory", "title": "Memory", "url": "memory.html", "text": "Vamp manages memory automatically. Strings, lists, maps, sets, objects and function values are released once nothing refers to them; a garbage collector finds them while the program runs. It runs only after a significant amount of new memory has been allocated (16 MB at first), so short loops never pause, and arithmetic, structs and function calls never involve it. When nothing else uses a string, list, map, set or object, free(value) releases it immediately; it must not be used afterwards. The memory library reports on and controls the collector: Call Result memory.Collect() Frees everything that is no longer used immediately. Useful between levels or after loading. memory.Used() Bytes currently used by Vamp values, as an int ."}, {"page": "Memory", "title": "Native memory", "url": "memory.html#native-memory", "text": "malloc(type, count) allocates native storage for a number of elements of any storable type (numbers, bool , char , str , structs). In most programs, a list is easier and safer. Copy val values = malloc ( int , 4 ) values [ 0 ] = 42 println ( values [ 0 ]) free ( values ) Pointer indexes are not bounds-checked. Initialize memory before reading it, stay within the allocated count, and call free exactly once. Do not use a pointer after freeing it."}, {"page": "Limits", "title": "Limits", "url": "limits.html", "text": "These limits were measured on Windows 11 with a 64-bit build. Exceeding any of them produces an error message rather than a silent crash. What Limit Recursion depth The main thread has a 64 MB stack, enough for about a million calls of a small function. Each thread.Start thread has 16 MB. Deeper recursion ends the program with Error: stack overflow . List length 2,147,483,647 values (memory permitting). Map and set size 536,870,912 entries. String length 2,147,483,647 bytes. Threads 1024 started threads that have not been joined. Join finished threads to start more. Integers int wraps around on overflow, as in C ( 9223372036854775807 + 1 is the smallest int ). Dividing the smallest int by -1 gives the smallest int . Nesting in source code At least 3,000 nested blocks, and expressions of about 30,000 terms. Deeper code produces a compile error asking for it to be split up. Regular expressions A pattern that takes too long to match (like (a+)+b on a long string) raises an error instead of hanging. JSON Documents nested more than 512 levels deep are rejected. Building a long string with text = text + piece in a loop copies the text every time. For thousands of pieces, use a builder or list.join , which are much faster. A crash that is not a Vamp error, such as accessing freed native memory, prints Error: invalid memory access and exits with code 1 ."}, {"page": "Standard libraries", "title": "Standard libraries", "url": "standard-libraries.html", "text": "Besides os , these libraries are built in. Import the ones you need; a program only includes the libraries it imports and calls. as and from ... import work with all of them. Copy import math import json as j from random import Int as roll"}, {"page": "math", "title": "math", "url": "standard-libraries-math.html", "text": "Every function accepts any number type. The result is a float , or an f32 if every argument was an f32 . Call Result math.Sqrt(x) , math.Pow(base, exponent) Square root and power. math.Sin(x) , math.Cos(x) , math.Tan(x) Trigonometry, in radians. math.Asin(x) , math.Acos(x) , math.Atan(x) , math.Atan2(y, x) Inverse trigonometry. math.Exp(x) , math.Log(x) , math.Log10(x) Exponential and logarithms. math.Floor(x) , math.Ceil(x) , math.Round(x) Rounding. The result is still a float , so use int(math.Floor(x)) for a whole number. math.Abs(x) , math.Min(a, b) , math.Max(a, b) , math.Clamp(x, low, high) When every argument has the same whole-number type, the result has that type too ( math.Max(3, 9) is the int 9 ). math.Lerp(a, b, t) a + (b - a) * t . math.Pi() 3.14159..."}, {"page": "random", "title": "random", "url": "standard-libraries-random.html", "text": "Call Result random.Int(low, high) A whole number from low to high , both included. random.Float() A float from 0.0 up to, but not including, 1.0 . random.Chance(probability) true with the given probability ( 0.25 is one in four). random.Seed(number) Makes the following numbers repeatable. Without it, every run differs."}, {"page": "time", "title": "time", "url": "standard-libraries-time.html", "text": "Call Result time.Millis() Milliseconds on a steady clock, as int . Subtract two readings to time something. time.Seconds() The same clock in seconds, as float . time.Now() Seconds since 1 January 1970 (UTC), as int . time.Year() , time.Month() , time.Day() , time.Hour() , time.Minute() , time.Second() Parts of the local date and time. time.Weekday() 0 for Sunday to 6 for Saturday. time.Format(pattern) Local date and time as text, using strftime codes: time.Format(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\") . time.Sleep(milliseconds) Waits. In a program with a window, use os.Sleep instead so the window stays responsive. time.Make(year, month, day, hour, minute, second) , time.Make_Date(year, month, day) A moment in local time as seconds since 1970 ( int ), like time.Now() . time.Format_Time(moment, pattern) A moment as text, same codes as time.Format . time.Parse(text, pattern) Reads a moment from text; understands %Y %m %d %H %M %S . Text that does not match raises an error. time.Year_Of(moment) , Month_Of , Day_Of , Hour_Of , Minute_Of , Second_Of , Weekday_Of Parts of a moment. time.Add_Days(moment, days) The same time of day, days later (or earlier when negative), handling month ends and daylight saving. time.Days_Between(from, to) Whole days between two dates."}, {"page": "file", "title": "file", "url": "standard-libraries-file.html", "text": "Call Result file.Read_Text(path) The whole file as a str . Raises an error if the file cannot be opened. file.Read_Lines(path) The file's lines as a list[str] . file.Write_Text(path, text) Creates or replaces the file. Returns whether it was written. file.Append_Text(path, text) Adds to the end of the file, creating it if needed. Returns whether it was written. file.Exists(path) Whether a file (not a folder) exists. file.Remove(path) , file.Rename(from, to) , file.Copy(from, to) Return whether the operation succeeded. Copy replaces an existing target. file.Size(path) Size in bytes as int , or -1 . Relative paths are resolved from the program's working directory. Folders are handled by the os library."}, {"page": "console", "title": "console", "url": "standard-libraries-console.html", "text": "Call Result console.Read_Line() Waits for a line typed by the user and returns it without the line ending. console.Read_Int() , console.Read_Float() Reads a line and converts it; text that is not a number gives 0 . console.Write(text) Prints without a new line (same as print ). console.Write_Error(text) Prints a line to the error output. console.Clear() Clears the console window. console.Set_Color(color) Text color 0 to 15 from the classic console palette ( 10 green, 12 red, 14 yellow, 15 white); -1 restores the default. console.Set_Title(title) Sets the console window's title. console.Flush() Forces pending output to appear."}, {"page": "json", "title": "json", "url": "standard-libraries-json.html", "text": "A JSON document is a value of type json . Values inside it are reached with a path: names separated by dots, and [index] for array elements. An empty path \"\" refers to the document itself. Copy import json val save = json . Load ( \"save.json\" ) val name : str = json . Get_Str ( save , \"player.name\" ) val hp : int = json . Get_Int ( save , \"player.hp\" ) val first_item : str = json . Get_Str ( save , \"player.items[0]\" ) json . Set_Int ( save , \"player.hp\" , hp - 10 ) json . Append_Str ( save , \"player.items\" , \"key\" ) json . Save ( save , \"save.json\" ) free ( save ) Call Result json.Parse(text) , json.Load(path) A document from text or from a file. Invalid JSON raises an error with the line and column. json.New_Object() , json.New_Array() A new, empty document. json.To_Text(doc) , json.To_Pretty_Text(doc) The document as compact or indented text. json.Save(doc, path) Writes indented JSON to a file; returns whether it was written. json.Has(doc, path) Whether a value exists at the path. json.Type(doc, path) \"object\" , \"array\" , \"string\" , \"number\" , \"bool\" , \"null\" , or \"missing\" . json.Length(doc, path) The number of elements in an array or members in an object. json.Keys(doc, path) An object's member names, as a list[str] . json.Get_Str , json.Get_Int , json.Get_Float , json.Get_Bool (doc, path) The value at the path. A missing path or a value of another kind raises an error. Get_Str also accepts numbers and booleans and returns them as text. json.Get_Str_Or , json.Get_Int_Or , json.Get_Float_Or , json.Get_Bool_Or (doc, path, fallback) The value, or fallback when it is missing or of another kind. json.Get(doc, path) The object or array at the path as a json value for further calls. It is part of doc and must not be freed. json.Set_Str , json.Set_Int , json.Set_Float , json.Set_Bool (doc, path, value) Sets the value, creating missing objects along the path. For arrays, an index equal to the length adds an element. json.Set_Null , json.Set_Object , json.Set_Array (doc, "}, {"page": "thread", "title": "thread", "url": "standard-libraries-thread.html", "text": "Copy import thread val done : int = 0 val lock : int = thread . Make_Lock () func work ( amount : int ) : ( thread . Lock ( lock ) done += amount thread . Unlock ( lock ) ) val first : int = thread . Start ( work , 1 ) val second : int = thread . Start ( work , 2 ) thread . Join ( first ) thread . Join ( second ) println ( done ) Call Result thread.Start(function) Runs a function that has no parameters on a new thread. Returns the thread's number. thread.Start(function, value) The same, for a function with one int parameter, which receives value . thread.Join(thread) Waits until the thread has finished. Returns false if the number is not a running or unjoined thread. thread.Running(thread) Whether the thread is still running. thread.Sleep(milliseconds) Pauses the current thread. thread.Make_Lock() A new lock, as an int . thread.Lock(lock) , thread.Unlock(lock) Only one thread at a time can hold a lock; the others wait in Lock . thread.Current_Id() The Windows id of the current thread. Threads share global variables, lists and maps, so hold a lock while changing anything another thread uses. The program ends when its main code ends, even if threads are still running, so Join the ones that must finish. An error that a thread does not catch ends the whole program."}, {"page": "net", "title": "net", "url": "standard-libraries-net.html", "text": "Copy import net val connection : int = net . Connect ( \"example.com\" , 80 ) if ( connection == 0 ) : ( throw ( \"could not connect\" ) ) net . Send ( connection , \"GET / HTTP/1.0 \\n Host: example.com \\n\\n \" ) println ( net . Receive ( connection , 4096 )) net . Close ( connection ) println ( net . Http_Get ( \"https://example.com/\" )) Call Result net.Connect(host, port) Opens a TCP connection. Returns its number, or 0 on failure. net.Listen(port) Starts accepting TCP connections on a port. Returns the listener's number, or 0 . net.Accept(listener) Waits for a client and returns a connection to it, or 0 . net.Send(connection, text) Sends all of the text. Returns the number of bytes sent, or -1 . net.Receive(connection, limit) Waits for data and returns up to limit bytes; \"\" when the other side has closed the connection. net.Close(connection) Closes a connection or listener. net.Http_Get(url) Downloads an http or https address and returns the body as text. Raises an error on failure. net.Download(url, path) Downloads to a file; returns whether it succeeded. net.Http_Post(url, body, content_type) Sends body to an http or https address and returns the reply, e.g. net.Http_Post(url, json.To_Text(doc), \"application/json\") . Raises an error on failure. net.Set_Timeout(connection, milliseconds) Makes Receive and Send give up after the given time ( Receive then returns \"\" ). Returns whether it was set. Accept and Receive wait, so a server usually runs them on a thread. Data is text, and a zero byte ends a received string."}, {"page": "regex", "title": "regex", "url": "standard-libraries-regex.html", "text": "Patterns use the common regular-expression syntax: . any character, [abc] and [^a-z] sets, \\d \\w \\s (and \\D \\W \\S ) for digits, word characters and whitespace, ^ and $ for start and end, \\b a word boundary, ( ) groups, (?: ) non-capturing groups, a|b either one, and the repeats * + ? {n} {n,} {n,m} (add ? after a repeat for the shortest match). In a Vamp string the backslash is doubled: \"\\\\d+\" . Call Result regex.Matches(pattern, text) Whether the whole text matches. regex.Contains(pattern, text) Whether the pattern appears anywhere in the text. regex.Find(pattern, text) The first match, or \"\" . regex.Find_All(pattern, text) Every match, as a list[str] . regex.Groups(pattern, text) For the first match: the whole match, then each group, as a list[str] . Empty when nothing matches. regex.Replace(pattern, text, replacement) Replaces every match. $1 to $9 in the replacement insert groups, $$ is a dollar sign. regex.Split(pattern, text) The pieces between matches. Copy import regex println ( regex . Groups ( \"( \\\\ w+)@( \\\\ w+) \\\\ .com\" , \"mail emma@example.com\" )) // [\"emma@example.com\", \"emma\", \"example\"] println ( regex . Replace ( \"( \\\\ w+) ( \\\\ w+)\" , \"hello world\" , \"$2 $1\" )) // world hello An invalid pattern raises an error that describes the problem. Patterns are compiled once and reused."}, {"page": "memory", "title": "memory", "url": "standard-libraries-memory.html", "text": "See Memory ."}, {"page": "input", "title": "input", "url": "standard-libraries-input.html", "text": "input reads the keyboard and mouse directly, whether or not the program's window has focus. Call Result input.Key_Down(key) Whether the key is currently held down. input.Key_Pressed(key) true once each time the key is pressed. Call it every frame. input.Mouse_Down(button) button is \"left\" , \"right\" or \"middle\" . input.Mouse_X() , input.Mouse_Y() Mouse position on the screen, in pixels. input.Mouse_Window_X(title) , input.Mouse_Window_Y(title) Mouse position inside the window with that exact title, or -1 when there is no such window. A key is a letter ( \"A\" ), a digit ( \"7\" ), or one of \"SPACE\" , \"ENTER\" , \"ESCAPE\" , \"TAB\" , \"BACKSPACE\" , \"DELETE\" , \"INSERT\" , \"LEFT\" , \"RIGHT\" , \"UP\" , \"DOWN\" , \"HOME\" , \"END\" , \"PAGEUP\" , \"PAGEDOWN\" , \"SHIFT\" , \"CTRL\" , \"ALT\" , \"LSHIFT\" , \"RSHIFT\" , \"LCTRL\" , \"RCTRL\" , \"CAPSLOCK\" , \"PLUS\" , \"MINUS\" , \"COMMA\" , \"PERIOD\" , \"F1\" to \"F12\" . Letter case does not matter. An unknown name is an error. Copy import os import input val window = os . Make_Window ( \"Game\" ) val x : int = 100 while ( ! input . Key_Down ( \"ESCAPE\" )) : ( if ( input . Key_Down ( \"LEFT\" )) : ( x -= 4 ) if ( input . Key_Down ( \"RIGHT\" )) : ( x += 4 ) os . Sleep ( 16 ) )"}, {"page": "audio", "title": "audio", "url": "standard-libraries-audio.html", "text": "Call Result audio.Play(path) Plays a WAV file in the background. A new sound replaces the one playing. Returns false if the file does not exist. audio.Play_Loop(path) Plays a WAV file repeatedly until audio.Stop() . audio.Play_Wait(path) Plays a WAV file and waits until it has finished. audio.Stop() Stops the sound started by Play or Play_Loop . audio.Beep(frequency, milliseconds) A simple tone; waits until it ends. audio.Play_Music(path) , audio.Loop_Music(path) Plays an MP3 or WAV as music, once or repeating. Music plays alongside audio.Play sounds. Returns whether it started. audio.Pause_Music() , audio.Resume_Music() , audio.Stop_Music() Control the music. audio.Set_Music_Volume(percent) 0 (silent) to 100 . One sound and one music track can play at the same time."}, {"page": "The os library", "title": "Files and folders", "url": "the-os-library.html#files-and-folders", "text": "Call Description os.Make_Directory(path) Creates the folder and any missing parent folders. Returns 0 on success or a Windows error code. os.Get_Directory(path) The absolute path of an existing folder; relative paths start from the working directory. On failure, it prints an error and returns \"\" . os.List_Directory(path) Prints the folder's entries one per line, omitting . and .. . Returns the entry count, or -1 on failure. os.Remove_Directory(path) Deletes a folder and its contents. Returns whether it succeeded. os.Directory_Exists(path) Whether the path exists and is a folder."}, {"page": "The os library", "title": "Programs, arguments and the environment", "url": "the-os-library.html#programs-arguments-and-the-environment", "text": "Call Result os.Args() The command line as a list[str] . The first entry is the program itself. os.Get_Env(name) An environment variable, or \"\" if it is not set. os.Set_Env(name, value) , os.Env_Exists(name) Sets a variable for this program and the programs it starts; checks whether one exists. os.Run(command) Runs a command (as in the Windows command prompt), waits for it, and returns its exit code. Its output appears in the console. os.Run_Output(command) The same, but returns everything the command printed. os.Start_Process(command) Starts a command without waiting and returns its process number. os.Process_Running(id) , os.Wait_Process(id) , os.Kill_Process(id) Whether it is still running; wait for it and get its exit code; stop it. Copy import os val args = os . Args () if ( args . length () > 1 ) : ( println ( \"first argument: \" + args [ 1 ]) ) println ( os . Run_Output ( \"git --version\" ))"}, {"page": "The os library", "title": "Windows", "url": "the-os-library.html#windows", "text": "Copy val opened = os . Make_Window ( \"Demo\" , ( icon = \"assets/app.png\" , size = ( 800 , 600 ), resizable = true , type = \"Windowed\" )) os.Make_Window(title, settings) creates a native Windows window and returns true on success. The settings are optional; the default is a resizable 800×600 window. Supported settings: icon = \"path\" : an ICO, PNG or JPEG, resolved from the working directory (the folder the program runs from). Any str expression can be used. If the icon cannot be loaded, a warning is printed and the window opens without it. size = (width, height) : positive whole numbers. resizable = true or false . type = \"Windowed\" , \"Full Screen\" , \"Maximized\" or \"Borderless\" . style = \"classic\" , \"native\" (default) or \"modern\" : the appearance of the controls. See Interface styles . theme = \"light\" , \"dark\" or \"system\" : the colors of a \"modern\" window, including the title bar. \"system\" follows the Windows app theme. Only valid with style = \"modern\" . Other window functions: Call Description os.Launch_Window(executable_path) Starts another program. Returns true if Windows accepts the launch. os.Remove_Window(title) Sends a close request to every visible window with that title; returns whether a request was sent. os.Get_Window(title) Whether a visible window with the matching title exists. os.List_Windows() Prints the titles of visible windows and returns their count. os.Sleep(milliseconds) Waits while still handling messages for Vamp windows. Use it to pace a loop. A negative duration prints an error and does not wait. os.Set_Window_Title(title, new_title) Renames the first visible window with that title; returns whether a window was renamed. A window created by the program remembers its original title, so its interface calls continue to use it. os.Resize_Window(title, width, height) Sets the outer size in pixels (both must be positive). Position and stacking are unchanged. Returns whether the window was resized. os.Move_Window(title, x, y) Moves the top-left corne"}, {"page": "Interface styles", "title": "Interface styles", "url": "interface-styles.html", "text": "Every window draws its controls in one of three styles, similar to Python's tkinter, ttk and CustomTkinter: Style Look \"classic\" The legacy Windows look: flat grey buttons, bold system font, labels on grey boxes. \"native\" The default. Themed Windows 10/11 controls in Segoe UI, as in most Windows applications. Labels sit directly on the window and text boxes have a border. \"modern\" Flat, rounded controls drawn by Vamp, CustomTkinter style: blue buttons that darken on hover and press (with a hand cursor), rounded text boxes that light up when focused, rounded frames, and a light or dark theme. Copy val window = os . Make_Window ( \"App\" , ( size = ( 480 , 320 ), style = \"modern\" , theme = \"dark\" )) val save = os . Make_Interface ( \"button\" , \"App\" , \"save\" , ( size = ( 140 , 36 ), position = ( 20 , 20 ), text = \"Save\" // accent blue in the modern theme )) val delete = os . Make_Interface ( \"button\" , \"App\" , \"delete\" , ( size = ( 140 , 36 ), position = ( 180 , 20 ), text = \"Delete\" , background_color = \"#c0392b\" , // custom colors still apply corner_radius = 18 // half the height: a pill shape )) val name = os . Make_Interface ( \"label\" , \"App\" , \"name\" , ( size = ( 300 , 34 ), position = ( 20 , 76 ), editable = true // a rounded text box )) val legacy = os . Make_Interface ( \"button\" , \"App\" , \"legacy\" , ( size = ( 140 , 36 ), position = ( 20 , 130 ), text = \"Old look\" , style = \"classic\" // one control can use a different style )) The window's style is the default for its controls, and a control's own style overrides it. A window that sets style needs its title as a string literal. corner_radius (whole pixels, 0 for square) works on modern controls. Defaults: 6 for buttons, text boxes and labels with a background, 8 for frames. In the modern style every control has theme colors, so text_color , background_color and background_transparency are optional. When set, they replace the theme colors, and os.Set_Interface_Text_Color and the other setters work on every modern "}, {"page": "Native interface controls", "title": "Native interface controls", "url": "native-interface-controls.html", "text": "os.Make_Interface puts controls in a Vamp window. The window must be created first. The window title and control name must be string literals, and names must be unique within a window. Copy import os val window = os . Make_Window ( \"Search\" ) val search = os . Make_Interface ( \"label\" , \"Search\" , \"query\" , ( size = ( 260 , 36 ), position = ( 20 , 20 ), text = \"\" , editable = true , text_color = \"#202020\" , text_transparency = 1.0 , background_color = \"#FFFFFF\" , background_transparency = 1.0 , font = \"Segoe UI\" , text_size = 16 , visible = true )) val submit = os . Make_Interface ( \"button\" , \"Search\" , \"submit\" , ( size = ( 100 , 36 ), position = ( 20 , 66 ), text = \"Search\" , visible = true )) The call has this form: Copy os . Make_Interface ( type , window_title , name , ( properties ...)) It returns true if the control was created. The parent must be a window created by the running program with os.Make_Window . Control types are \"label\" , \"button\" , \"frame\" , \"icon\" and \"canvas\" (see Drawing on a canvas ). size and position are required whole-number pairs, in pixels from the window's top-left corner. visible is optional and defaults to true ."}, {"page": "Native interface controls", "title": "Properties by control type", "url": "native-interface-controls.html#properties-by-control-type", "text": "Property label button frame icon size , position , visible , layer , group , style Yes Yes Yes Yes corner_radius (modern style) Yes Yes Yes Yes text Yes Yes No No icon No Optional No Required editable Optional No No No text_color , text_transparency , font , text_size Yes Yes No No background_color , background_transparency Yes Yes Yes Yes An editable label is a text-entry field. A button requires exactly one of text or icon . Buttons with custom background settings are drawn by Vamp so the background can be blended; buttons without them are standard Windows buttons. icon is an image path (required for an icon control), resolved from the working directory. Windows and controls support ICO, PNG and JPEG images. layer is a whole number, 0 by default. When controls overlap, higher layers are drawn in front, regardless of creation order. style and corner_radius are covered in Interface styles . Colors are \"#RRGGBB\" strings. Fonts are Windows font names, and text_size is a positive size in pixels. background_transparency goes from 0.0 (fully transparent) to 1.0 (fully opaque, the default when background_color is set); values in between set the opacity, so 0.9 is 90% opaque. The background is composited over whatever lies behind it. text_transparency works the same way and is controlled separately. Copy val panel = os . Make_Interface ( \"frame\" , \"Search\" , \"panel\" , ( size = ( 300 , 160 ), position = ( 0 , 0 ), layer = 0 , background_color = \"#000000\" , background_transparency = 1.0 )) val overlay = os . Make_Interface ( \"label\" , \"Search\" , \"overlay\" , ( size = ( 180 , 60 ), position = ( 20 , 20 ), layer = 1 , text = \"Overlay\" , background_color = \"#FF0000\" , background_transparency = 0.5 )) Clicks can be checked in a loop: Copy while ( true ) : ( if ( os . Interface_Clicked ( \"Search\" , \"submit\" )) : ( val query = os . Get_Interface_Text ( \"Search\" , \"query\" ) println ( query ) ) os . Sleep ( 16 ) ) os.Interface_Clicked(window_title, name) returns true once for every c"}, {"page": "Changing, querying, and removing interfaces", "title": "Changing, querying, and removing interfaces", "url": "changing-querying-and-removing-interfaces.html", "text": "Every control created with os.Make_Interface can be changed afterwards. Like the creation call, each function takes the window title and control name as string literals, and the control must belong to a window created by the program. Copy import os val window = os . Make_Window ( \"Search\" ) val status = os . Make_Interface ( \"label\" , \"Search\" , \"status\" , ( size = ( 260 , 36 ), position = ( 20 , 20 ), text = \"Ready\" , background_color = \"#FFFFFF\" , background_transparency = 1.0 )) os . Set_Interface_Text ( \"Search\" , \"status\" , \"Searching...\" ) os . Set_Interface_Text_Color ( \"Search\" , \"status\" , \"#0e9e86\" ) os . Set_Interface_Background_Transparency ( \"Search\" , \"status\" , 0.5 ) os . Set_Interface_Position ( \"Search\" , \"status\" , 20 , 60 ) println ( os . Get_Interface_Width ( \"Search\" , \"status\" )) Call Description os.Get_Interface(window_title, name) Whether the control exists. os.Set_Interface_Text(window_title, name, text) Replaces a label's or button's text. text can be any string expression. os.Set_Interface_Visible(window_title, name, visible) Shows or hides the control. os.Set_Interface_Enabled(window_title, name, enabled) Enables or disables the control. A disabled button no longer reports clicks. os.Set_Interface_Editable(window_title, name, editable) Allows or blocks typing in a label created with editable = true . os.Set_Interface_Position(window_title, name, x, y) Moves the control, in pixels from the window's top-left corner. os.Set_Interface_Size(window_title, name, width, height) Resizes the control. Both values must be positive. os.Set_Interface_Layer(window_title, name, layer) Changes its layer and reorders it using the same rules as creation. os.Set_Interface_Text_Color(window_title, name, color) Text color of a label or button; color is a \"#RRGGBB\" literal. os.Set_Interface_Background_Color(window_title, name, color) Background color as a \"#RRGGBB\" literal. Keeps the current transparency. os.Set_Interface_Background_Transparency(window_title, n"}, {"page": "Interface groups", "title": "Interface groups", "url": "interface-groups.html", "text": "A group is a named set of controls in one window, such as a HUD or a pause menu. Group functions act on every control in the group at once, so switching screens does not require listing each control. A control is added to a group with the group property at creation, or later with os.Set_Interface_Group : Copy import os import input val window = os . Make_Window ( \"Game\" ) val score = os . Make_Interface ( \"label\" , \"Game\" , \"score\" , ( size = ( 120 , 30 ), position = ( 10 , 10 ), text = \"Score: 0\" , group = \"hud\" )) val lives = os . Make_Interface ( \"label\" , \"Game\" , \"lives\" , ( size = ( 120 , 30 ), position = ( 10 , 45 ), text = \"Lives: 3\" , group = \"hud\" )) val resume = os . Make_Interface ( \"button\" , \"Game\" , \"resume\" , ( size = ( 160 , 40 ), position = ( 320 , 200 ), text = \"Resume\" , visible = false , group = \"pause\" )) val quit = os . Make_Interface ( \"button\" , \"Game\" , \"quit\" , ( size = ( 160 , 40 ), position = ( 320 , 250 ), text = \"Quit\" , visible = false , group = \"pause\" )) val paused : bool = false while ( true ) : ( if ( input . Key_Pressed ( \"ESCAPE\" ) and not paused ) : ( paused = true os . Switch_Interface_Group ( \"Game\" , \"pause\" ) // show the pause menu, hide the HUD ) if ( os . Interface_Clicked ( \"Game\" , \"resume\" )) : ( paused = false os . Switch_Interface_Group ( \"Game\" , \"hud\" ) ) if ( os . Interface_Clicked ( \"Game\" , \"quit\" )) : ( exit ( 0 ) ) os . Sleep ( 16 ) ) Call Description os.Make_Interface_Group(window_title, group) Declares an empty group. This is not needed for a group already used in a group property or os.Set_Interface_Group . Returns true . os.Set_Interface_Group(window_title, name, group) Moves the control into the group, leaving its previous group. An empty name \"\" removes it from every group. Returns whether the control exists. os.Interface_In_Group(window_title, name, group) Whether the control is currently in the group. os.Show_Interface_Group(window_title, group) , os.Hide_Interface_Group(window_title, group) Shows or h"}, {"page": "Events", "title": "Events", "url": "events.html", "text": "Instead of a polling loop, a program can attach functions to events and let os.Run_Events() call them. It runs until every window the program created is closed, or until os.Stop_Events() is called. Copy import os val window = os . Make_Window ( \"Counter\" , ( style = \"modern\" )) val counter = os . Make_Interface ( \"label\" , \"Counter\" , \"count\" , ( size = ( 200 , 30 ), position = ( 20 , 20 ), text = \"0\" )) val more = os . Make_Interface ( \"button\" , \"Counter\" , \"more\" , ( size = ( 120 , 34 ), position = ( 20 , 60 ), text = \"Add one\" )) val clicks : int = 0 os . On_Click ( \"Counter\" , \"more\" , func () : ( clicks += 1 os . Set_Interface_Text ( \"Counter\" , \"count\" , str ( clicks )) )) os . On_Key ( \"ESCAPE\" , func () : ( os . Stop_Events () )) os . Every ( 1000 , func () : ( println ( f\"{ clicks } clicks so far\" ) )) os . Run_Events () Call Description os.On_Click(window_title, name, function) Calls function each time the button is clicked. os.On_Key(key, function) Calls function each time the key is pressed (same key names as the input library, as a string literal). os.Every(milliseconds, function) Calls function repeatedly at the given interval. os.Run_Events() , os.Stop_Events() Start handling events; stop and continue after Run_Events() . The functions are func () values, either named functions or functions written inline. Calling On_Click again for the same button replaces its function."}, {"page": "Drawing on a canvas", "title": "Drawing on a canvas", "url": "drawing-on-a-canvas.html", "text": "A canvas control is a drawing surface for games, charts and custom controls. Drawing goes to a hidden image that appears when os.Present is called, so a frame is never shown half drawn. Copy import os val window = os . Make_Window ( \"Game\" , ( size = ( 520 , 400 ) )) val screen = os . Make_Interface ( \"canvas\" , \"Game\" , \"screen\" , ( size = ( 480 , 320 ), position = ( 10 , 10 ), background_color = \"#101820\" )) val x : int = 0 os . Every ( 16 , func () : ( x = ( x + 4 ) % 480 os . Canvas_Clear ( \"Game\" , \"screen\" , \"#101820\" ) os . Fill_Circle ( \"Game\" , \"screen\" , x , 160 , 20 , \"orange\" ) os . Draw_Text ( \"Game\" , \"screen\" , 10 , 10 , f\"x = { x }\" , \"white\" , 16 ) os . Present ( \"Game\" , \"screen\" ) )) os . Run_Events () Call Description os.Canvas_Clear(window, name, color) Fills the whole canvas. os.Fill_Rect / os.Draw_Rect(window, name, x, y, width, height, color) A filled or outlined rectangle. os.Draw_Line(window, name, x1, y1, x2, y2, color) A line. os.Fill_Circle / os.Draw_Circle(window, name, x, y, radius, color) A filled or outlined circle centred on (x, y) . os.Draw_Text(window, name, x, y, text, color, size) Text with its top-left corner at (x, y) . os.Draw_Image(window, name, path, x, y, width, height) A PNG, JPEG, BMP, GIF or ICO image scaled into the rectangle; returns whether it loaded. Images are loaded once and cached. os.Present(window, name) Shows what was drawn since the last Present . os.Save_Canvas(window, name, path) Saves the drawing as .png , .jpg or .bmp ; returns whether it succeeded. os.Canvas_Width(window, name) , os.Canvas_Height(window, name) The canvas size in pixels. Colors are \"#RRGGBB\" or one of \"black\" , \"white\" , \"red\" , \"green\" , \"blue\" , \"yellow\" , \"orange\" , \"purple\" , \"gray\" . Positions are pixels from the canvas's top-left corner, and drawing outside it is clipped. Shapes are written directly into the image's pixels, so thousands of shapes per frame are inexpensive. A canvas reports clicks like a button ( os.Interface_Clicked"}, {"page": "The vamp command", "title": "The vamp command", "url": "the-vamp-command.html", "text": "Command Description vamp file.vp Builds file.exe . vamp run file.vp [arguments] Builds and runs it with the given arguments (read them with os.Args() ). vamp test file.vp Runs the file's test blocks. vamp check file.vp Reports the first error without building; --json prints it for editors. vamp format file.vp Prints the file with tidy indentation; --write saves it. vamp symbols file.vp Lists the file's declarations as JSON, for editors. vamp install <git address> [name] , vamp remove name , vamp packages Manage packages. vamp setup Checks for LLVM (clang) and the Visual Studio C++ build tools, which Vamp requires to build programs, and installs any that are missing with winget . vamp setup --vscode Installs the Vamp extension in Visual Studio Code from the .vsix file next to vamp.exe . Add --debug to vamp file.vp or vamp run to build with debugging information: the program is built without optimization and a .pdb file is written next to the .exe ."}, {"page": "Editor support and debugging", "title": "Editor support and debugging", "url": "editor-support-and-debugging.html", "text": "The Vamp extension for Visual Studio Code highlights code and, through the vamp command, reports errors on save, shows declarations on hover, jumps to declarations (F12), completes names (including every library function after math. and similar prefixes), and formats files (Shift+Alt+F). It uses Compiler/main.py in the workspace, then the installed vamp.exe , then vamp on the PATH; the vamp.compiler setting selects a different command. Vamp: Run File , Vamp: Run Tests in File and Vamp: Build for Debugging are in the command palette. To debug, install Microsoft's C/C++ extension, open a .vp file, set breakpoints and press F5. The extension builds the file with --debug and runs it under the Visual Studio debugger; Ctrl+F5 runs it without the debugger. Breakpoints, stepping, the call stack, and local number, bool , char and str variables all work directly in the .vp source."}];
